# crack_baseline_v2 (2026-09-30) = retune iteration R3c. SUPERSEDED by crack_baseline_v3.env (R7a).
# (CHANGES.md item 14: composite SEI-on-cracks area bug). Supersedes crack_baseline_v1.
# ONE parameter set for both 25 and 45 degC; runs on the high_temp_45C fork via
# crack_growth_sweep.py. Everything not listed = fork defaults (SOLVENT_MULT=5,
# GR_ESEI=38000, SI_CRIT_STRESS=6e6, SI_LAM_EAC=40000, WIDTH=3e-4, Si-only aging deformations).
# Only the operating temperature and per-cell F0 (= experiment k at first RPT) differ:
#   25 degC: C64_T_AMBIENT_K=298.15 C64_F0=0.7   45 degC: C64_T_AMBIENT_K=318.15 C64_F0=0.8
# All *_EAC / SI_ESEI Arrhenius factors are exactly 1 at 298.15 K.
C64_SI_CRACK_MULT=1.0e3
C64_SI_CRACK_EAC=90000
C64_SI_ESEI=35000
C64_SI_TAU_LAM_ISO=3.5e8
C64_SI_LAM_ISO_EXPONENT=20
C64_SI_REDIRECT_LAM_YIELD=0.25
C64_SI_YIELD_EAC=35000
C64_GR_REDIRECT_TO_LAM=1
C64_GR_REDIRECT_LAM_YIELD=0.018
C64_GR_YIELD_EAC=43000
C64_GR_LAM_ISO_EXPONENT=10
C64_SI_STRESS_LAM_DAMP_EXP=0.25
C64_MAX_CYCLES=1800
